From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mariotaku <git@mariotaku.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] linux-user: getsockopt SO_PEERGROUPS

SO_PEERGROUPS fell through to the int case: qemu asked the kernel with a
4-byte buffer and, for a peer with more than one group, returned ERANGE
without the length the kernel had reported. systemd's getpeergroups()
grows its buffer by that length and asks again, so systemd as PID 1 under
qemu-arm spun at 100% CPU in that loop once a client with several groups
connected, and stopped answering systemctl.

Answer it as SO_PEERSEC is answered: the guest's buffer and length passed
to the host (gids are 32-bit on both), the length written back, ERANGE
included.
---
diff --git a/linux-user/generic/sockbits.h b/linux-user/generic/sockbits.h
index b3b4a8e44..3410d2a95 100644
--- a/linux-user/generic/sockbits.h
+++ b/linux-user/generic/sockbits.h
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@
 
 #define TARGET_SO_PEERSEC              31
 
+#define TARGET_SO_PEERGROUPS           59
+
 #define TARGET_SO_PROTOCOL             38
 #define TARGET_SO_DOMAIN               39
 #endif
diff --git a/linux-user/syscall.c b/linux-user/syscall.c
index 8ef4ed61e..d158724f6 100644
--- a/linux-user/syscall.c
+++ b/linux-user/syscall.c
@@ -2675,6 +2675,33 @@ get_timeout:
             unlock_user(name, optval_addr, lv);
             break;
         }
+#ifdef SO_PEERGROUPS
+        case TARGET_SO_PEERGROUPS: {
+            /*
+             * An array of 32-bit gids, as on the host; ERANGE with the length needed when it
+             * is too short, which callers (systemd's getpeergroups()) grow the buffer by.
+             */
+            void *gids;
+
+            if (get_user_u32(len, optlen)) {
+                return -TARGET_EFAULT;
+            }
+            if (len < 0) {
+                return -TARGET_EINVAL;
+            }
+            gids = lock_user(VERIFY_WRITE, optval_addr, len, 0);
+            if (!gids && len) {
+                return -TARGET_EFAULT;
+            }
+            lv = len;
+            ret = get_errno(getsockopt(sockfd, level, SO_PEERGROUPS, gids, &lv));
+            if (put_user_u32(lv, optlen)) {
+                ret = -TARGET_EFAULT;
+            }
+            unlock_user(gids, optval_addr, ret < 0 ? 0 : lv);
+            break;
+        }
+#endif
         case TARGET_SO_LINGER:
         {
             struct linger lg;
